  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "The average (mean) of \\(20\\) numbers is \\(30,\\) and the average of \\(30\\) other numbers is \\(20.\\) What is the average of all \\(50\\) numbers?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(23\\)",
    "B": "\\(24\\)",
    "C": "\\(25\\)",
    "D": "\\(26\\)",
    "E": "\\(27\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "To combine the averages, first recover each group’s sum by multiplying its average by its number of values. The first group has sum \\(20\\cdot30=600\\), and the second has sum \\(30\\cdot20=600\\).\n\nAll \\(50\\) numbers therefore have sum \\(1200\\), giving an average of\n\\[\n\\frac{600+600}{20+30}=\\frac{1200}{50}=\\boxed{24}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\text{B}\\).",
